  "about": "The introitus of the formulary “Third Sunday after Easter” in the 1962 Roman Missal.",
  "segments": {
    "s01": { "translation": "Shout for joy to God, all the earth, alleluia; sing a psalm to His name, alleluia; give glory to His praise, alleluia, alleluia, alleluia. Say to God: How awesome are Your works, O Lord! Through the greatness of Your power Your enemies will lie to You. Glory be to the Father, and to the Son, and to the Holy Spirit. As it was in the beginning, is now, and ever shall be, world without end. Amen. Shout for joy to God, all the earth, alleluia; sing a psalm to His name, alleluia; give glory to His praise, alleluia, alleluia, alleluia.", "alignments": [{ "words": ["w039", "w040"], "anchor": "w039", "gloss": "to the Holy Spirit" }, { "words": ["w050", "w051", "w052"], "anchor": "w051", "gloss": "forever and ever" }] }
